                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "Bot",
                    "login": "gemini-code-assist"
                  },
                  "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nWhile the logic is correct, the formatting of this multi-line conditional expression can be improved for better readability and adherence to PEP 8 style guidelines.[^1] Using a standard `if ... else` structure and enclosing the expression in parentheses makes the code clearer and easier to maintain.\n\n```suggestion\n        (\n            model.shared_embedding_or_output_weight()\n            if model.share_embeddings_and_output_weights\n            else model.output_layer.weight\n        ),\n```\n\n#### Style Guide References\n[^1]: According to PEP 8, the preferred way of wrapping long lines is by using Python's implied line continuation inside parentheses. For conditional expressions, it's recommended to use a clear structure that enhances readability.",
