  "reviews": [
    {
      "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request correctly addresses a critical `AttributeError` that occurs when using a fused kernel with shared embeddings. The fix ensures that the correct weight tensor is passed to `linear_cross_entropy`, preventing the crash. The change is well-targeted and the explanation is clear.\n\nWhile reviewing, I noticed a similar code pattern in `verl/models/mcore/model_forward_1f1b_overlap.py` where `linear_cross_entropy` is called with `self.output_layer.weight` directly. This could lead to the same bug under similar conditions. It would be beneficial to investigate and potentially apply a similar fix in that file as well to ensure consistency and prevent future issues.",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pull/4174#pullrequestreview-3475243597",
      "id": 3475243597,
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "submitted_at": "2025-11-18T02:34:50Z",
